<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Frederick, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1700–1739</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Frederick, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp, lost the ducal part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/schleswig">Schleswig</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a>, a loss confirmed in 1720. He found support in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and married Anna Petrovna, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>. Their son became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Peter III, linking the house of Holstein-Gottorp to the Russian throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-frederick-duke-of-holstein-gottorp.jpg" alt="Charles Frederick, Duke of Holstein-Gottorp" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Charles_Frederick_of_Holstein-Gottorp_by_anonymous_(Kuskovo,_18th_c.).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
